  <event id="203">
      <start>17:50</start>
      <duration>00:30</duration>
      <room>AW1.120</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>A common graph database access layer for .NET/Mono</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Mono devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A common graph database access layer for .NET/Mono&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Within the NoSQL landscape graph database are becoming a more and more&#xA;considerable choice for managing complex interconnected data. Unfortunately there had not been very much vendor interoperability yet.&#xA;The Tinkerpop projects started to overcome these limitations and today&#xA;provide a common graphdb access layer and toolset within the Java world.&#xA;But Blueprints.NET, rexster.NET and pipes.NET are not only ports of these Java libraries to the .NET / Mono platform, they exceed them by making a heavy use of latest developments like the Dynamic Language Runtime and the Task Parallel Library. The talk will give a short overview on the basics of graph databases, the porting and developing efforts of the libraries and present several cool applications for graph databases based on these libraries.&lt;/p&gt;      </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2031">Achim Friedland</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>